Subject: [PATCH] dwindle, master: don't lay out an expired target (crash on exit)

For Hyprland v0.55.2 (39d7e20). Applies on top of astroland's
hyprland_clamp_to_border.patch too (that one only touches src/render).

Hyprland 0.55.2 segfaults when it quits (hl.dsp.exit(), or SIGTERM: a
logout, `systemctl stop`) with two or more tiled windows open in the dwindle
or the master layout:

  #0 Layout::ITarget::setPositionGlobal(CBox const&)
  #1 Layout::Tiled::C{Dwindle,Master}Algorithm::calculateWorkspace()
  #2 Layout::Tiled::C{Dwindle,Master}Algorithm::removeTarget(SP<ITarget>)
     ... CSpace::remove <- ITarget::assignToSpace <- CLayoutManager::removeTarget
  #7 Desktop::View::CWindow::unmapWindow()
     ... CXDGSurfaceResource destroyed <- wl_client_destroy
 #19 wl_display_destroy_clients
 #20 CCompositor::cleanup()

At that point a window has only two strong owners: CCompositor::m_windows,
and the renderer's render pass from the last frame (every CSurfacePassElement
holds a PHLWINDOW; the pass is only cleared by the next beginRender()).
CCompositor::cleanup() clears m_windows before wl_display_destroy_clients().
When the first client is destroyed, its window unmaps, and unmapWindow()
makes a snapshot of it. The snapshot's beginRender() clears the render pass,
which drops the last reference to every other window. Those windows are
destroyed right there, without unmapWindow(). ~CWindow() doesn't take a
window's target out of its layout, so its node stays, with an expired
pTarget (a WP<ITarget>). unmapWindow() then calls removeTarget(), and
calculateWorkspace() calls setPositionGlobal() through the expired pointer,
with a null `this`. (Windows the last frame didn't draw are already freed
by m_windows.clear() and leave dead nodes the same way.)

dwindle: the source hunk of upstream 338bdbb3 ("dwindle: avoid crashing on
expired weakptr", #15415, Tom Englund, first released in v0.56.0), without
its hyprtester change.

master: the same guard in CMasterAlgorithm::calculateWorkspace(), which
upstream main (e368c13c) still lacks. It covers every setPositionGlobal() on
a node's pTarget (the single master, two master-column loops, three stack
loops), and the warpPositionSize() loop of the function's scope guard. That
last one is reached only from resizeTarget(), not from cleanup, but it's the
same pattern, so it's guarded too. As with 338bdbb3, an expired node still
takes its slot in the arithmetic. That only happens during teardown, or
transiently, as 338bdbb3's commit message describes.

Scrolling and monocle don't crash (tested). The plugin API hash is the git
commit's, and this doesn't change it, so plugins built for 0.55.2 keep
loading.

